  "complete_discussion": "All four selected Seed0 roles complete their original protocols. K15 and K20 keep the same two qualified proofs as old D1 and stock, with production 27.488248 / 86.671444 s and total 32.645135 / 95.985987 s. Against historical R141 D1 their production gains are 4.871086 / 6.864130 s, below the inherited max(10 s,10% of the smaller clock) threshold. K20 versus historical stock improves production by 14.963941 s, which is substantive, but total by only 8.473685 s, below 10 s. This is a cross-version whole-method comparison, not an isolated CP timing claim. K35 ends at U/L=0.665418889072/0.545040775489; its old-D1 changes are U +0.009869163281 and L -0.014489358147. RB35-T2 ends at 0.357402102170/0.229365546910, a repair over historical old D1 but still a worse U/stronger L tradeoff against stable GI-TBC, and worse at both endpoints than old TC+stock and TC2+stock. K35 is also dominated by old TC+stock. All open certificate times stay null; no cap is called convergence.",
  "attribution_discussion": "Two independently paid same-PE old-D1 bridges retain the identical source/PE, input, own H, root, selection/pivot, count links and complete window. The first integer matrices match after removing only the floor row; source CP is absent from those integer models. K20 old D1 produces its proof in 87.545767 s (97.476894 total); selected CP changes production by -0.874323 s and total by -1.490906 s, without a substantive incremental proof-clock gain. RB old D1 ends at U/L=0.413773275022/0.227903449004; CP improves both endpoints, with U delta -0.056371172852 and L delta 0.001462097906. This is the actual matched complete intervention: stronger source models and the returned two floor coefficients. It does not identify Native branching on b or attribute the result only to the weak-side raw objective increment. K35 has no new same-PE bridge; retain its adverse cross-version comparison without assigning causality solely to CP. Native returned bounds and the externally merged supported L remain separate full-table fields.",
  "decision_paragraph": "Retain the uniform selected-CP entry as research-only and close this count-proof continuation. Conditional count products fill a real shared-factor relaxation freedom and raise all three weaker sources/min-covers. They do not provide a sufficiently consistent complete-method increment for promotion: the small-role old-D1 proof benefit is not substantive under same-PE matching, K35 regresses at both endpoints against historical D1, and the hard roles remain behind old TC+stock at both endpoints. Stable R137 GI-TBC remains the default. Preserve the actual RB matched result and every adverse/failed result as finite research evidence; neither stronger LPs nor this panel proves general Native performance dominance.",
  "conditional_work_discussion": "The independently selected K20/RB same-PE bridges are complete. No remaining-four-role expansion, new D0 grid or Seed1 is entered: these would not change the adoption/stop decision given the completed hard-role boundary. No missing role is inferred. ALL has no useful extra source information, reverse inventory bounds are implied and unchanged, and further similar RLT, AM/Seed grids or H redesign are not opened. A future continuation needs genuinely different joint information or search evidence, under a new explicit task. Stopping is based on scientific and marginal decision value with ample unused budget, not the 8-hour ceiling.",
